---

Body tracking uses the stance crate (https://github.com/divotmaker/stance),
whose `pose` module contains code ported from rtmlib
(https://github.com/Tau-J/rtmlib) by Tau-J and contributors, licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0: the RTMPose pre- and post-processing
(box to crop, affine warp, normalization, SimCC decoding), the YOLOX output
decoding and non-maximum suppression, and the detect-every-N-frames pose
tracking scheme.

That code derives in turn from:

- MMPose (https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmpose), Copyright 2018-2020
  Open-MMLab (OpenMMLab), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  the RTMPose box-to-crop, top-down affine and SimCC decoding. OpenMMLab
  also publishes the RTMPose weights body tracking loads.
- YOLOX (https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX), Copyright (c)
  2021-2022 Megvii Inc., licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:
  the YOLOX grid decoding and non-maximum suppression. Megvii also
  publishes the YOLOX weights body tracking loads.

The pose models are not part of flighthook. They are downloaded separately
on first use; their licenses are listed in docs/devices/cameras.md.
